      },
      "message": "fix(post): Fanuc, Haas, Mazak, 840D and Doosan DNM state the mm unit before any motion\n\nThese five mill posts always write millimetre numbers but wrote no unit\nword, so a control left in inch by power-on or the last program read\nevery coordinate 25.4x too long. Each now states the unit it writes in\nits opening block: G21 in a block of its own at the end of onOpen\n(Fanuc, Haas, Mazak, Doosan DNM), and G710 (metric lengths and feeds)\nin the 840D's section opening block, so its N numbering is unchanged.\n\nThe posts do not read machine.units and refuse nothing: where the\nprogram's unit is chosen, and inch output, is #902 (maintainer scope\nchange on the issue). Goldens change only by the new word; the\nmacro_b probe reader models G21; regression line counts +1.\n\nPinned by post_unit_word (one test per post).\n\nFixes #901\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
